WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.102
Tucker Carlson is out at Fox News.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.870
The network saying in a statement, quote,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.138
We thank him for his service

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.606
to the network as a host and prior

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.608
to that as a contributor.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.242
That was it.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:09.609
The surprise

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.177
announcement coming just a week after Fox

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.812
News settled a defamation lawsuit

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.481
with Dominion voting systems

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:15.715
for more than three quarters

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:16.950
of $1,000,000,000.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.550
That lawsuit

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.251
revealed text

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.786
between Carlson and staffers

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:20.320
where he said that

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.855
he hated for President

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.923
Trump despite saying other things on air.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.225
Texts also showing him

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.326
making disparaging comments

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.827
about Fox executives.

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.896
Joining us now on this is CNN senior

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.098
senior media reporter Oliver Darcy

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:32.565
and CNN

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.566
political commentator

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:34.501
Jonah Goldberg, who

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.269
we should note left Fox News

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.771
after being there for 12 years

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:38.671
when Carlson said

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:39.172
that January

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.474
six was a false flag operation.

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.843
Thank you both for being here.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.844
All right.
I think the question

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:45.412
this morning

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:46.980
that even Tucker may be asking

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.615
himself is why?

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:50.550
Why now Why is the big question?

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.385
And that's just unclear, to be honest.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.686
At this point in time,

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.021
I think it's impossible

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.424
to disconnect the decision for Fox News

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.526
from the Big Dominion settlement

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.226
last week.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:00.727
I mean,
that was

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:04.230
a massive settlement, $787.5 million.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.765
They had a payout to Dominion.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.333
It's it's unclear exactly, though,

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.768
what part of that lawsuit

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.703
I think, factored into Carlson's

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.238
ultimate firing at Fox News.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.206
There are a number of factors

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.407
that could have factored in,

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.108
but it's unclear

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.910
exactly what was its undoing

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.211
as related to that lawsuit.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.045
But we should keep in mind

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.514
that the Murdochs had stood by Carlson

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.682
through everything.

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.250
I mean, he made white nationalist

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.351
remarks on Fox News.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.019
They stood by him.

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:26.586
He made

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.954
and to make certain remarks,

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:28.655
they stood by him.

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:29.322
He promoted

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.123
conspiracy theories

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.357
about the COVID vaccines.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:32.192
They stood by him.

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:32.959
He promoted

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.227
conspiracy theories and truther

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.995
ism about the January six attack.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:36.596
They stood by him.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.431
He so did about the 2020 election.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.265
And they stood by him.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.835
So something changed in their calculus.

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:42.368
And it's

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.170
perhaps it was just that the risk versus

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.673
the reward calculation had altered.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.942
And he was just costing them

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.376
too much problems

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.245
and not offering enough reward.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.146
And they just decided

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.248
maybe to just wipe their hands clean.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:55.715
Yeah.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.283
Jonah, I mean, as someone who didn't

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.985
stand by him, right?

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.721
You know, you've known him for 12 years.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:02.422
You worked at

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.524
you were a contributor there to Fox News.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.426
I wonder what you think

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.961
the final straw could have been.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:10.763
Yeah, just be clear.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:11.364
I knew Tucker.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.799
I've known Tucker for 25 years.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.033
I mean, I knew more

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.001
or he went to Fox News.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:15.702
Yeah.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:16.569
Yeah.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:18.338
And but regardless, Well,

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:19.506
I think Oliver's right.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.541
I think that it's still kind of opaque

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:23.376
and murky about what?

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:23.710
You know,

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:24.177
there's a reason

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.812
why we call the last straw.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:26.646
The last straw,

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:27.714
because normally straws

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:30.150
don't break camel's backs, right?

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.352
But it's all the stuff prior to the straw

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.554
that makes it the decisive factor.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:37.023
I do think that there is

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:37.857
you know, the L.A.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.893
Times where I write a column, there's a

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.094
there there

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.929
apparently it's the Abby Grossberg Tapes

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.164
or Abby Grossberg lawsuit.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:44.731
Something about

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.766
that is a big part of the decision

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.636
And also something about

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:52.105
the Rae Epps episode on 60 Minutes,

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.740
which sort of debunk

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.742
Tucker's false flag operation stuff.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.510
And I think that one of the things

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.545
that a lot of people don't understand

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:00.113
is that Tucker's schtick,

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.748
where he called January

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.516
six this false flag thing,

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.250
where he leans

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.152
into all these conspiracy theories.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.353
That's actually related

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:08.388
to the Dominion suit.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:11.057
And in a sort of weird way insofar as

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:13.092
that whole idea of

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.260
respecting the audience,

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.129
if you follow that logic

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:16.796
where you say, well,

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:17.564
we should tell the audience

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:19.365
what it wants to hear,

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.733
why go half assed with that?

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:21.935
Go all in. Right.

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:23.903
And that's
what Tucker did, is rather than just say,

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:24.671
oh, maybe there's something

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:25.939
to this Dominion thing,

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.340
He said, no, no, no, no.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.374
These deplorable people

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:29.409
who stormed the Capitol,

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:30.643
they're actually heroes

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.412
and victims and martyrs.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:34.714
And he really force fed

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.182
and pandered to the audience

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.650
what he thought it wanted to hear,

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.119
not just this sort of half measure.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.221
You know, let's say

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:43.289
Trump is got something going.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.557
Maybe it maybe onto something

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.124
with his Dominion

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:46.759
the stuff he said, no, no, no.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.294
Let's take the worst things

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.230
about Trump and January six

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.931
and turn them into positives for us

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:52.232
because that's

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.400
what the audience really wants to hear.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.301
And the thing about that

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.303
is it's a really big audience.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:57.670
Oliver,

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.805
I mean, he was one of the highest

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:01.307
rated anchors that they had.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:02.408
And I think that's why, you know,

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:03.810
the front page of The New York Times

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:04.644
and the Washington Post,

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.713
it was your a one in your newsletter.

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:07.614
And so the question is

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.148
what does that look like going forward?

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.950
Because obviously,

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.151
I've heard from people in Trump world,

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.087
they're stunned by this. He was a big

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:15.822
conservative.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.790
If you
wanted to be a successful Republican,

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.025
you had to go on his show.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.326
Essentially, people felt

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.361
I think there are two questions

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:22.061
about what's next.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.229
What's next for Fox News

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:25.832
and what's next for the Republican Party

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.200
moving forward? For Fox?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.434
For the Republican Party, I think.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.003
Well, I think for the Republican Party,

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:30.970
you had Tucker Carlson,

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.106
who really shaped the modern day GOP

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.941
and he pushed it to the extremes.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:35.775
I mean, Tucker Carlson

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:37.677
was not your average conservative.

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:38.344
He made

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.113
Sean Hannity look fairly moderate

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.114
on a lot of positions.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.482
He was an extremist

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.150
and he whipped the Republican Party

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.251
in that direction.

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:46.986
And so without him doing that,

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.721
without GOP lawmakers

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:49.422
fearing that

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:49.956
if they didn't

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.224
say the right thing,

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:52.392
that Tucker Carlson would

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:54.027
go on his April time

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.895
perch and lash out at them.

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.930
I think that, you know, really

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:58.698
it doesn't

00:04:58.698 --> 00:04:59.999
we don't know what's going to happen.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:02.201
I mean,
I think this is going to change the GOP

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:03.536
in some way.

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:05.305
And I think for Fox News,

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:06.272
they have some problems

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:07.240
as well, potentially,

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:07.640
if Tucker

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.208
Carlson decides to go somewhere else.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.477
They were really worried after

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:12.645
the 20, 20 election

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:13.713
about losing an audience

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:16.049
to the smaller competitors like Newsmax

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:17.183
if Tucker Carlson somehow

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.618
turns up on one of those channels

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:20.753
or does his own thing. It's not.

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:22.088
I mean, it would not be,

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:22.922
you know, unheard of.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.624
That a significant chunk of his audience

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:25.692
could follow him.

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:26.793
So I think those are the two things

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.861
I'm watching right now.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:29.762
Jonah, as someone who's done

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:31.564
Tucker for 25 years

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:34.634
and worked at Fox for 12, do you I mean,

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.402
no world in which

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:38.604
this is the end of Tucker Carlson in the

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:39.639
in the

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:41.941
in the public eye on some media platform,

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.142
maybe his own

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:45.845
Yeah.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.680
I think there's a very real possibility

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:48.414
he goes full.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.783
Joe Rogan creates his own thing.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:54.654
Then he gets to do things on his terms.

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:55.488
He will definitely want

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:56.689
to get the last word

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:58.591
or at least get his version of events.

00:05:58.591 --> 00:05:59.425
He may be

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:00.126
he may be in

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.627
need of lawyering up right now

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:02.795
because of the Grossberg stuff.

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:03.830
Who knows?

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.198
But I think it's absolutely true.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:06.299
We haven't seen the last of

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:07.233
Tucker Carlson.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.368
I do think it's important,

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:10.636
you know,
in this Republican Party question,

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:11.037
you know,

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:11.637
we call it

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:12.338
Ron DeSantis,

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:15.675
one of the first missteps he had was

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:16.843
he felt

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:18.945
compelled to fill out Tucker Carlson's

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:21.547
campaign questionnaire.

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:22.982
And that's where he called, you know,

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.784
the Ukraine stuff, a border dispute.

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:26.018
None of these candidates know

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.387
GOP people are going to feel compelled

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:28.254
to fill out

00:06:28.254 --> 00:06:29.822
whoever replaces Tucker

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:30.857
in his questionnaire.

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:32.725
Yeah,
that's such a

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:33.359
good point, Jonah,

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:35.094
because it does show just the impact

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:35.895
that he had, that

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:37.063
what they did was they just reached out

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:37.764
to all these candidates

00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:39.298
to ask for their position on Ukraine

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:40.633
and then read them live on air.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:42.368
Basically, what was didn't do it.

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:43.102
A major. Yeah.

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:44.470
And then I later retroactively

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.539
did a major moment for dissenters there.

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:47.707
We'll see what the impact of this

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:48.741
looks like going forward.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:49.575
Jonah Goldberg,

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:50.910
Oliver Darcy, thank you both.

